stralia through eastern Asia to north of the Arctic Circle in Siberia, and support numerous rare and critically endangered bird species;* > > *(c) these wetlands fulfil criteria for eligibility to be listed under the Ramsar Convention to protect wetlands of international significance;* > > *(d) previous attempts to have this area Ramsar listed were supported by the Federal Government, however, were not progressed by the Tasmanian state government due to opposition from a few local landowners, who are potential financial beneficiaries of proposed developments in the area;* > > *(e) in their EPBC submission, proponents of the UPC wind farm noted their project 'will potentially intersect the nationally important Boulanger Bay - Robbins Passage wetland' but that the wetlands 'are not matters of national environmental significance for the purposes of environmental approvals'; and* > > *(f) if Ramsar listed, the area must be reviewed under any EPBC assessment.*","result":"negative","slug":"division-federal-senate-7044","source_url":"https://theyvoteforyou.org.au/divisions/senate/2021-03-17/1"}
